  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 2. Result\nFor the same global rotation on each site, $\\Phi_2=x_0\\,\\rho(g)^{\\otimes2}$ with $g\\leftrightarrow(w,y_1)$:\n$$\\frac{\\langle\\Phi_2|\\Psi_B\\rangle}{\\langle x_0|\\Psi_B\\rangle}\\ \\propto\\ \\underbrace{\\frac{\\det_{6\\times6}N[Q_B,Q_{{\\rm vac},w}]}{\\Psi_Q^B(x_0)}}_{\\langle\\Omega_{zw}|\\Psi\\rangle\\text{ formula}}\\ \\times\\ \\underbrace{\\frac{\\det_{4\\times4}\\big[-\\langle Q^jE\\,x^{\\beta-1}\\rangle_k,\\ \\langle Q^{j[-2]}E\\,x^{\\beta-1}\\rangle_k\\big]_{j\\in\\{3,2\\}}}{\\prod_s\\big[Q^2(\\theta_s-2h)Q^3(\\theta_s-3h)-Q^3(\\theta_s-2h)Q^2(\\theta_s-3h)\\big]}}_{=\\prod_i(1-z_i/y_1)^{-\\mu_i},\\ E=y_1^{-x/h}}$$\n- **Precision.** Each identity holds for all 64 states to about $10^{-50}$, for $y_1=-6/5$, $3$ and $5/7+i/3$.\n- **The su(2)-like factor is $4\\times4$, i.e. $2L\\times2L$.** Its rows are the two dual Q's $Q^3,Q^2$ times the two brackets $k$, and its columns are $\\{-\\langle PE\\rangle,\\langle P^{[-2]}E\\rangle\\}\\times\\{1,x\\}$.\n  - At L=1 it is $2\\times2$.\n  - It is the y₂→∞ degeneration of the $6\\times6$ vacuum determinant: $F_2\\to E$ on $\\{\\theta_s-2h,\\theta_s-h\\}$, checked directly. The column operation that removes the $F_1$ rows from the $\\langle PF^{[2]}\\rangle$ columns reduces it to $4\\times4$.\n- **No single-Q $2\\times2$.** None reproduces the factor; the best residual is 0.87.\n- **Not done.**\n  - Solving $(w,y_1)$ for a given L=2 target $g$ (the L=1 solve, Rotation-e8-SoV 10b, applies site by site).\n  - Explicit $c_0$-type normalizations: only state-independence is checked.\n  - A second numeric point.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 3. Rotation on site 1 only: $\\Phi=x_0^{(1)}\\rho(g)\\otimes x_0^{(1)}$\n**Step 1: localization.** For $T_\\lambda\\in\\{T_{10},T_{11},T_{20},T_{21}\\}$, built from the L=2 $t(z)$ by CBR at $\\theta_1-2h$, test whether\n$$(a\\otimes x_0^{(1)})\\,T_\\lambda^{L=2}(\\theta_1-2h)=f_\\lambda\\,(a\\,T_\\lambda^{L=1,\\theta_1}(\\theta_1-2h))\\otimes x_0^{(1)}$$\nholds for every site-1 covector $a$, with one constant $f_\\lambda$.\n\nIf so, the whole site-1 SoV algebra acts locally on $\\cdot\\otimes x_0^{(1)}$. The site-1 rotation is then $\\langle x_0|M^{(1)}$, with $M^{(1)}$ diagonal on $\\Psi_B$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* L=2 fused transfer matrices at v (CBR), diagonal twist z *)\ntZv[a_, v_] := tZ[[a]] /. u -> v;\nT2[{1, 0}, v_] := tZv[1, v]; T2[{1, 1}, v_] := tZv[2, v];\nT2[{2, 0}, v_] := tZv[1, v] . tZv[1, v + hN] - tZv[2, v + hN];\nT2[{2, 1}, v_] := tZv[2, v] . tZv[1, v + hN] - tZv[3, v + hN];\n(* one-site (site 1, θ1) transfer matrices with twist diag(z) *)\nL1m[i_, j_][v_] := KroneckerDelta[i, j] (v - thN[[1]]) IdentityMatrix[d1] + hN Ee[i, j];\nqm1[I_, J_][v_] := Sum[Signature[σ] Dot @@ Table[zN[[J[[k]]]] L1m[σ[[k]], J[[k]]][v - (k - 1) hN], {k, Length[J]}], {σ, Permutations[I]}];\nt1s[a_, v_] := Sum[qm1[I, I][v], {I, Subsets[Range[3], {a}]}];\nT1[{1, 0}, v_] := t1s[1, v]; T1[{1, 1}, v_] := t1s[2, v];\nT1[{2, 0}, v_] := t1s[1, v] . t1s[1, v + hN] - t1s[2, v + hN];\nT1[{2, 1}, v_] := t1s[2, v] . t1s[1, v + hN] - t1s[3, v + hN];\nv0 = thN[[1]] - 2 hN;\nlams = {{1, 0}, {1, 1}, {2, 0}, {2, 1}};\nT2n = Association[Table[l -> T2[l, v0], {l, lams}]]; T1n = Association[Table[l -> T1[l, v0], {l, lams}]];\n(* localization test on random site-1 covectors a (and on a = x0^(1)) *)\nSeedRandom[101];\nlocTest = Table[Module[{fs = {}, errs = {}},\n    Do[Module[{a = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, d1], lhs, rhs, f},\n       lhs = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[a, x01]] . T2n[l]; rhs = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[a . T1n[l], x01]];\n       f = (lhs . rhs)/(rhs . rhs); AppendTo[fs, f]; AppendTo[errs, Norm[N[lhs - f rhs, 30]]/Norm[N[lhs, 30]]]], {3}];\n    {l, Union[Simplify[fs]], Max[errs]}], {l, lams}];\nlocTest",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
