   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 4. Result: Q-function representation of the site-1 rotation\nIn the companion frame, write $x_0=e_1^T\\otimes e_1^T$ and $\\Phi=(e_1^T\\rho(g))\\otimes e_1^T$.\n\n**L=2 SoV basis.** The untwisted $B(u)$ has a simple spectrum on the 64 states. They form the full $8\\times8$ grid (site-1 root triple, site-2 root triple), each ladder carrying the 8 L=1 patterns.\n\n**L=2 SoV wavefunction**, exact for all 64 SoV states and all 64 eigenstates, $\\sim10^{-48}$, and for several row/$k$ choices:\n$$\\frac{\\langle x|\\Psi_B\\rangle}{\\langle x_0|\\Psi_B\\rangle}=N_x\\prod_{s=1,2}\\frac{\\det_2[v(x_{s,21}),v(x_{s,1})]\\,v_k(x_{s,22})}{(\\text{same at the vacuum roots }\\theta_s-3h,\\theta_s-2h,\\theta_s-h)},\\qquad v=(Q^1,Q^2,Q^3)\\text{ of the L=2 state}.$$\n\n**Expansion of $\\Phi$.** Only 12 SoV states appear:\n- the 8 states with site 2 at the vacuum roots;\n- 4 states with site 2 at $\\{2|20\\}$, where $x_{2,22}$ moves from $\\theta_2-h$ to $\\theta_2$. Their site-2 factor is $\\lambda_2(B)=v_k(\\theta_2)/v_k(\\theta_2-h)$, which does not depend on $k$ because $v(\\theta_2)\\parallel v(\\theta_2-h)$.\n\nThe result is\n$$\\frac{\\langle\\Phi|\\Psi_B\\rangle}{\\langle x_0|\\Psi_B\\rangle}=\\sum_{\\nu}c^{L=1}_\\nu(g)\\,W_\\nu(B),\\qquad W_\\nu(B)=\\sum_{x}K_{\\nu x}\\,\\psi^{(1)}_{x_1}(B)\\,\\lambda_2(B)^{[x_2\\neq{\\rm vac}]},$$\nwhere:\n- $c^{L=1}_\\nu(g)$ are the L=1 SoV coefficients of $e_1^T\\rho(g)$, i.e. the bilinear $c(a,b)$ of Rotation-e8-SoV Section 3;\n- $\\psi^{(1)}$ is the site-1 factor above, built from the L=2 Q's;\n- $K$ is $g$-independent, sparse and rational. In the normalization $K_{\\{2|21\\},\\rm vac}=1$:\n\n| $\\nu$ | (site-1 pattern; site-2 vac) | (·; site-2 $\\{2\\|20\\}$) |\n|---|---|---|\n| {2\\|21} | {2\\|21}: 1 | — |\n| {2\\|11} | {2\\|11}: 8/27, {2\\|20}: −35/124 | {2\\|21}: −3395/3348 |\n| {1\\|11} | {1\\|11}: −4/9 | — |\n| {2\\|20} | {2\\|20}: −1/2 | — |\n| {2\\|10} | {2\\|10}: −4/27 | {2\\|20}: 35/54 |\n| {2\\|00} | {2\\|00}: 1/31, {1\\|10}: 35/108 | {2\\|10}: −35/124 |\n| {1\\|10} | {1\\|10}: 2/9 | — |\n| {1\\|00} | {1\\|00}: −3/62 | {1\\|10}: −35/558 |\n\n**Reading the table.**\n- At $h=1/2$ and $\\theta_{12}=31/35$, the 31s and 35s are $t=\\theta_{12}/h=62/35$. The site-2 coupling is therefore rational in $t$.\n- The four $\\nu$ with a single entry are exactly those for which $x_\\nu\\otimes e_1^T$ is already a B-eigencovector.\n\n**Open.**\n- The closed form of $K$ in $t$, which needs a second numeric point.\n- Whether $\\sum_\\nu c_\\nu(w,y_1)W_\\nu$ resums to a compact determinant, e.g. ladder-1 brackets of the L=2 Q's times the su(2)-like factor, as it does at L=1.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 5. Toward a compact det form: ladder-dependent bra data\n- **Idea.** $\\det N$ only probes $F$ at the points $\\theta_s+mh$ ($m=-2,\\dots,1$) of each ladder, so $F$ can be chosen differently on the two ladders. This is the same as inserting polynomials that kill some ladder poles.\n- **Ansatz.** For a rotation on site 1 only, put the twist data on ladder 1 and \"SoV-vacuum\" data $F_0$ on ladder 2.\n- **Step 1.** Find $F_0$ such that $\\det_6[Q_B,F_0]/\\Psi_Q(x_0)$ is state-independent, i.e. it reproduces $x_0$ itself. Scan $F_1,F_2$ supported on single points $m_1,m_2$, the same on both ladders.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "onPt[x_, m_] := Or @@ Table[Abs[x - (thN[[s]] + m hN)] < 10^-30, {s, nL}];\nladOf[x_] := First[Select[{1, 2}, Function[s, Min[Table[Abs[x - (thN[[s]] + m hN)], {m, -4, 2}]] < 10^-30]], {0}];\nFdelta[m1_, m2_] := Function[{i, x}, Which[i == 1, If[onPt[x, m1], 1, 0], i == 2, If[onPt[x, m2], 1, 0], True, 0]];\nconstQ[vals_] := If[Max[Abs[vals]] < 10^-40, Infinity, Max[Abs[vals/vals[[1]] - 1]]];\nscanF0 = Flatten[Table[{m1, m2, constQ[Table[det6[B, Fdelta[m1, m2]]/psiQ[B], {B, nS}]]}, {m1, -2, 1}, {m2, -2, 1}], 1];\nSortBy[N[scanF0, 3], Last][[1 ;; 5]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
