  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* the solution set is a 2-parameter family (5 null directions = 3 gauges + 2). Pick F2 = δ_{θ2} on ladder 2 and solve for F1 there (F1(θ2-2h) = 1 fixes its scale) *)\nsolveF1[TT_] := Module[{d6c, r, J, it, st, f1u},\n   f1u = {1, a1, a2, a3};\n   d6c = d6sym /. Thread[unk -> Join[f1u, {0, 0, 1, 0}]];\n   r[v_, l_] := (d6c /. Thread[{a1, a2, a3} -> v]) - l TT;\n   J = Transpose[Join[Transpose[D[d6c, {{a1, a2, a3}}]], {-TT}]];\n   Block[{$MinPrecision = 60, $MaxPrecision = 60},\n    it = NestList[Function[s, Module[{Jn = J /. Thread[{a1, a2, a3} -> s[[1]]], dx}, dx = -PseudoInverse[Jn, Tolerance -> 10^-30] . r @@ s; {s[[1]] + dx[[1 ;; 3]], s[[2]] + dx[[4]]}]], {SetPrecision[{0.13, 0.28, -0.02}, 60], SetPrecision[(d6c /. Thread[{a1, a2, a3} -> {0.13, 0.28, -0.02}]) . TT/(TT . TT), 60]}, 25];\n    {Last[it], Norm[r @@ Last[it]]/Norm[TT]}]];\n{solF1, resF1} = solveF1[TA];\nchecks[\"Ω_w⊗e1: ladder 2 = (F1 = (1,a1,a2,a3), F2 = δ_θ2) solves all 64\"] = resF1;\n{N[resF1, 3], N[solF1[[1]], 15]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
