     ],
     "id": "59ba3e66-dada-49be-8cc0-99e2bc3bcb9c"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result 5b: RETRACTED.**\n- **The claim.** The \"genuine\" claim, the \"second-$w$ check\" ($10^{-56}$) and the \"rank drop\".\n- **Why it was wrong.** All of these were the trivial solution: $\\lambda\\approx0$ and $\\det\\equiv0$. The rank-6 counting argument did not exclude it, because $\\lambda=0$ satisfies every equation.\n- **Correct test.** See 6b, which fixes $\\lambda=1$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 6. Pinning down $F^{(2)}$\n**6a. Is $F^{(2)}$ independent of $w$?** Solve the $w$ and $w'$ systems simultaneously for one common $F^{(2)}$, with two separate scales $\\lambda,\\lambda'$: 128 equations.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* joint Gauss-Newton: unknowns = 8 ladder-2 values + lambda + lambda' *)\nresJ[vals_, l1_, l2_] := Join[(d6sym /. Thread[unk -> vals]) - l1 TA, (d6sym2 /. Thread[unk -> vals]) - l2 TA2];\njacJ = Join[Transpose[Join[Transpose[D[d6sym, {unk}]], {-TA, 0 TA}]], Transpose[Join[Transpose[D[d6sym2, {unk}]], {0 TA2, -TA2}]]];\njointFit = Block[{$MinPrecision = 60, $MaxPrecision = 60}, Module[{best = {Infinity}, st, it, r},\n    Do[st = {SetPrecision[If[k == 1, ladder2Sol[[1]], ladder2Sol[[1]] + RandomReal[{-1, 1}, 8]/(2 k)], 60], ladder2Sol[[2]], 1};\n     st[[3]] = With[{d = d6sym2 /. Thread[unk -> st[[1]]]}, (d . TA2)/(TA2 . TA2)];\n     it = Nest[Function[s, Module[{J = jacJ /. Thread[unk -> s[[1]]], dx}, dx = -PseudoInverse[J, Tolerance -> 10^-30] . (resJ @@ s); {s[[1]] + dx[[1 ;; 8]], s[[2]] + dx[[9]], s[[3]] + dx[[10]]}]], st, 40];\n     r = Norm[resJ @@ it]/Norm[Join[TA, TA2]]; If[r < best[[1]], best = {r, it}], {k, 6}]; best]];\nchecks[\"6a: one F^(2) for both w and w' (joint residual)\"] = jointFit[[1]];\nN[jointFit[[1]], 3]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"485294\" data-output-id=\"165\" data-out-n=\"2101\" data-sub-idx=\"5\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"36\" data-sub-start=\"9\" data-sub-end=\"9\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[2101]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"MS4xM1x0aW1lcyAxMF57LTQ2fQ==\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.13</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8641em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8641em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">46</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[2101]= 1.13\\times 10^{-46}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "c9aa5c93-df1d-4c3a-9af4-b11a80aec789"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* fast characterization of S: on ladder 2 the det is linear in F2. For given ladder-2 F1 (4 values), build A[B,m] = det6L with F2 = δ_m and test whether\n   sum_m A[B,m] c_m = λ T_B has a solution: smallest singular value of [A | -T] (64 x 5), for the w and w' targets together *)\nF1F2lad2[f1_, m2_] := Function[{i, x}, Which[i == 1, Sum[If[Abs[x - (thN[[2]] + m hN)] < 10^-30, f1[[m + 3]], 0], {m, -2, 1}], i == 2, If[Abs[x - (thN[[2]] + m2 hN)] < 10^-30, 1, 0], True, 0]];\nAmat[f1_, Fl1_] := Table[det6L[B, {Fl1, F1F2lad2[f1, m2]}]/psiQ[B], {B, nS}, {m2, -2, 1}];\nallowF1[f1_] := Module[{A1 = Amat[f1, Fvac], A2 = Amat[f1, Fvac2], M, sv},\n   M = ArrayFlatten[{{A1, -Transpose[{TA}], 0 Transpose[{TA}]}, {A2, 0 Transpose[{TA2}], -Transpose[{TA2}]}}];\n   sv = SingularValueList[M, 6, Tolerance -> 0]; {sv[[-1]]/sv[[1]], NullSpace[M, Tolerance -> 10^-35]}];\n(* the known solution's F1 should be allowed; F1 = δ_{θ2-2h} (the vacuum-like F1) and a random F1 for comparison *)\nf1known = ladder2Sol[[1, 1 ;; 4]];\n{t0, res0} = AbsoluteTiming[allowF1[f1known]];\n{N[t0, 3], N[res0[[1]], 3], N[allowF1[{1, 0, 0, 0}][[1]], 3], N[allowF1[{1, 1/3, -2/5, 1/7}][[1]], 3]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"485294\" data-output-id=\"167\" data-out-n=\"2111\" data-sub-idx=\"7\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"37\" data-sub-start=\"10\" data-sub-end=\"10\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[2111]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"XGxlZnRcezAuODAzNDc5LDcuNDJcdGltZXMgMTBeey02Nn0sMCwyLjcxXHRpbWVzIDEwXnstNjV9XHJpZ2h0XH0=\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.2141em;vertical-align:-0.35em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\"><span class=\"delimsizing size1\">{</span></span><span class=\"mord\">0.803479</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">7.42</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8641em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">66</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2.71</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8641em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">65</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\"><span class=\"delimsizing size1\">}</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[2111]= \\left\\{0.803479,7.42\\times 10^{-66},0,2.71\\times 10^{-65}\\right\\}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "26503e04-9053-4ade-ba24-eba09e796621"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 6b. RETRACTION and redo\n**The Section 5 \"solution\" was the trivial branch.** All the fitted $F^{(2)}$ had $\\lambda\\approx0$ and $\\det_6\\equiv0$: $F_2$ sat in the gauge direction $F_2\\propto F_1$, so the $F_2$ row duplicated an $F_1$ row. The objective $|\\det_6-\\lambda T|$ with $\\lambda$ free admitted this. The \"2-parameter family\", \"$w$-independence\" and \"rank drop\" were all properties of the trivial branch. **The claimed 6×6 for $\\Omega_w\\otimes e_1^T$ is not established.**\n\n**Redo with the scale fixed.** Set $\\lambda=1$. This is allowed because the det is quadratic in the ladder-2 $F_1$, so $F_1$'s scale absorbs $\\lambda$. For each $F_1$ the best $F_2$ is then a linear least-squares problem. The bilinear coefficient tensors are precomputed by polarization (exact, 60 digits), and the residual is minimized over $F_1$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* A[B,m](F1) = sum_{a<=b} F1_a F1_b C[a,b][B,m]: polarization from 10 exact evaluations *)\nAex[f1_] := Amat[f1, Fvac];\nCdiag = Table[Aex[UnitVector[4, a]], {a, 4}];\nCoff = Table[If[a < b, Aex[UnitVector[4, a] + UnitVector[4, b]] - Cdiag[[a]] - Cdiag[[b]], 0], {a, 4}, {b, 4}];\nAfast[f1_] := Sum[f1[[a]]^2 Cdiag[[a]], {a, 4}] + Sum[f1[[a]] f1[[b]] Coff[[a, b]], {a, 4}, {b, a + 1, 4}];\nchecks[\"6b: polarized A(F1) = direct A(F1)\"] = With[{f = {1, 1/3, -2/5, 1/7}}, Max[Abs[Flatten[Afast[f] - Aex[f]]]]/Max[Abs[Flatten[Aex[f]]]]];\n(* residual of the best F2 for given F1, with lambda = 1 *)\nresFast[f1_?(VectorQ[#, NumericQ] &)] := Module[{A = Afast[SetPrecision[f1, 50]], c}, c = LeastSquares[A, TA]; Norm[A . c - TA]/Norm[TA]];\nSeedRandom[211];\nfitsTrue = Table[Module[{st = RandomReal[{-2, 2}, 4], sol}, sol = Quiet[FindMinimum[resFast[{p1, p2, p3, p4}], Transpose[{{p1, p2, p3, p4}, st}], WorkingPrecision -> 40, MaxIterations -> 300, Method -> \"PrincipalAxis\"]]; {sol[[1]], {p1, p2, p3, p4} /. sol[[2]]}], {8}];\nchecks[\"6b: min over F1 of the lambda=1 residual (nonzero = no such 6x6)\"] = Min[fitsTrue[[All, 1]]];\n{N[checks[\"6b: polarized A(F1) = direct A(F1)\"], 3], N[Sort[fitsTrue[[All, 1]]], 3]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<details class=\"vscode-wolfram-message-output\" style=\"color:#f44;border-left:3px solid #f44;background:rgba(255,68,68,0.08);padding:2px 6px;margin:1px 0;border-radius:0 3px 3px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:0.85em\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer\">8 warnings</summary><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">FindMinimum::lsbrak: Unable to bracket a minimum along the direction {-2.149602603317056780168515834613230619449 10  , -1.375223329784175953953122393057821972611 10  , 8.920591350787580250671938804341210843380 10  , 2.401922012523905927332694427880128593396 10  } from the point {-3.037924103701875177256451541725225083230, -1.943523378838184873508012193146644211906, 2.975292226851494591008682202443429890913, 0.7124885796344846914628111584893967488495}.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">FindMinimum::lsbrak: Unable to bracket a minimum along the direction {-2.149602603317056780168515834613230619449 10  , -1.375223329784175953953122393057821972611 10  , 8.920591350787580250671938804341210843380 10  , 2.401922012523905927332694427880128593396 10  } from the point {-3.037924103701875177256451541725225083230, -1.943523378838184873508012193146644211906, 2.975292226851494591008682202443429890913, 0.7124885796344846914628111584893967488495}.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">FindMinimum::lsbrak: Unable to bracket a minimum along the direction {-2.149602603317056780168515834613230619449 10  , -1.375223329784175953953122393057821972611 10  , 8.920591350787580250671938804341210843380 10  , 2.401922012523905927332694427880128593396 10  } from the point {-3.037924103701875177256451541725225083230, -1.943523378838184873508012193146644211906, 2.975292226851494591008682202443429890913, 0.7124885796344846914628111584893967488495}.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">General::stop: Further output of FindMinimum::lsbrak will be suppressed during this calculation.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">ReplaceAll::reps: {p1, 1.90853} is neither a list of replacement rules nor a valid dispatch table, and so cannot be used for replacing.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">ReplaceAll::reps: {p2, -1.93278} is neither a list of replacement rules nor a valid dispatch table, and so cannot be used for replacing.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">ReplaceAll::reps: {p3, 0.726493} is neither a list of replacement rules nor a valid dispatch table, and so cannot be used for replacing.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">General::stop: Further output of ReplaceAll::reps will be suppressed during this calculation.</div></details>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
