  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result 7 (Direction 1): negative.**\n- **Validation.** The fast determinant reproduces det6L ($10^{-51}$), and the adjugate Jacobian matches finite differences ($10^{-33}$).\n- **Free data on both ladders.** With $F^{(1)},F^{(2)}$ free (16 numbers, $\\lambda=1$ fixed), Levenberg–Marquardt from 4 natural and 40 random starts, then 300 extra steps on the best 6, plateaus at a minimal relative residual of **0.273**. Every run gives 0.27–0.28, with $\\|\\det\\|/\\|T\\|\\approx0.96$, so this is not the trivial branch.\n- **X-relaxation** (the bridge to Direction 3). For fixed $F_1$'s, replacing $F_2^{(1)}\\otimes F_2^{(2)}$ by a general $4\\times4$ $X$ gives a reachable space of rank only 9 (out of 64). The residual is 0.269 at the best $F_1$'s and 0.61–0.92 at the natural ones ($F_w$, $F_0$).\n- **Conclusion.** No per-ladder $6\\times6$, not even a sum of such determinants sharing the ladder-1 $F_1$ data, reproduces $\\langle\\Omega_w\\otimes e_1^T|\\Psi\\rangle$.\n- **Implication.** The per-ladder bracket structure itself must change, through column insertions (Direction 2) or different determinant shapes, or the answer is a genuine sum over SoV states (Direction 4).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 8. Direction 2: polynomial insertions (plan: `site1-Qform/2-polynomial-insertions.md`)\n**General framework.** Each bracket integrand carries a weight $W[k,f,p]$:\n- $k\\in\\{1,2\\}$ labels the bracket;\n- $f$ labels the column type: $-\\langle PF\\rangle$, $\\langle PF^{[2]}\\rangle$ or $\\langle P^{[-2]}F\\rangle$;\n- $p$ runs over the 6 poles.\n\nThe matrix entry is $\\sum_pW[k,f,p]\\,x_p^{\\beta-1}G_f^{(i,j)}(B,p)$. The natural brackets have $W=\\mathrm{wgt}_p\\,\\mathrm{ins}_k(x_p)$, and a polynomial insertion multiplies this by $\\pi_{k,f}(x_p)$. The bra data stay natural: the $w$-vacuum Q's.\n\n**Target and safeguard.** The target is $T_A=\\langle\\Omega_w\\otimes e_1^T|\\Psi\\rangle/\\langle x_0|\\Psi\\rangle$. Only state-independent ratios with $\\det\\not\\equiv0$ count.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* per-pole contributions G[B, ij, f, p] with F = w-vacuum Q's (or F0) *)\nGof[F_] := Table[With[{x = xP[p], i = ij[[1]], j = ij[[2]]}, N[{-QU[B, j, x] F[i, x], QU[B, j, x] F[i, x + hN], QU[B, j, x - hN] F[i, x]}, prec]], {B, nS}, {ij, prsL1}, {p, poles}];   (* 64 x 3 x 6 x 3(f) *)\nGw = Gof[Fvac]; G0 = Gof[F0];\nxPv = N[xP /@ poles, prec];\n(* W[[k, f, p]]: 2 x 3 x 6; rows (ij; k), columns (f, beta) in rowFb order *)\nmatW[G_, B_, W_] := Flatten[Table[Table[Sum[W[[k, f, p]] xPv[[p]]^(be - 1) G[[B, ij, p, f]], {p, 6}], {f, 3}, {be, 2}] // Flatten, {k, 2}, {ij, 3}], 1];\ndetW[G_, W_] := Table[Det[matW[G, B, W]]/psiQv[[B]], {B, nS}];\nWnat = Table[N[wgt[poles[[p]]] ins[k][xP[poles[[p]]]], prec], {k, 2}, {f, 3}, {p, 6}];\nchecks[\"8: Wnat reproduces the 6x6 for Ω_w⊗Ω_w and x0\"] = {constQ[Table[(Flatten[KroneckerProduct[Ωc[wN], Ωc[wN]]] . ketC[[B]])/(x0C . ketC[[B]]), {B, nS}]/detW[Gw, Wnat]], constQ[detW[G0, Wnat]]};\n(* Stage 1: kill masks on ladder-2 poles (poles 4,5,6 = ladder 2, n = 0,1,2), same mask for all columns of a bracket *)\nmaskW[m1_, m2_] := Table[Wnat[[k, f, p]] If[p > 3, {m1, m2}[[k]][[p - 3]], 1], {k, 2}, {f, 3}, {p, 6}];\nmasks = Tuples[{0, 1}, 3];\nstage1 = Flatten[Table[Module[{d = detW[Gw, maskW[m1, m2]], d0 = detW[G0, maskW[m1, m2]]},\n     {m1, m2, Norm[d]/Norm[TA], If[Norm[d] < 10^-40, Infinity, constQ[TA/d]], If[Norm[d0] < 10^-40, Infinity, constQ[d0]]}], {m1, masks}, {m2, masks}], 1];\n{N[checks[\"8: Wnat reproduces the 6x6 for Ω_w⊗Ω_w and x0\"], 3], N[Take[SortBy[stage1, #[[4]] &], 6], 3]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
