   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result 9 (Direction 3): negative for short sums.**\n- **Natural dictionary.** 56 nonzero atoms: ladder-1 data in {$F_w$, $F_w^{L=1}$, 16 delta types}, ladder-2 data in {$F_w$, 16 delta types}.\n  - The span has rank 55 < 64, and even the full least-squares fit leaves $9.6\\cdot10^{-4}$.\n  - With ladder 1 fixed to $F_w$ (7 atoms), the residual is 0.70.\n  - Greedy sparse selection descends only slowly: 0.67, 0.60, 0.51, 0.49, 0.44, …\n- **Unrestricted sums.** The 1600 polarized per-ladder atoms span all 64 dimensions, so *some* sum of per-ladder determinants always exists. The meaningful question is the minimal number of terms.\n- **Two free determinants** (32 numbers, $\\lambda=1$). 8 starts plus 2000 extra steps on the best: the residual creeps from 0.117 to 0.107. The two terms are each about 5.5–6 times $\\|T\\|$ and growing slowly, i.e. they largely cancel. This is a stuck, cancellation-driven fit, not a solution.\n- **Conclusion.** With these brackets, $\\langle\\Omega_w\\otimes e_1^T|\\Psi\\rangle$ is not a natural short sum, and not a sum of two free per-ladder $6\\times6$'s either.\n- **Overall (Directions 1–3).** Within the per-ladder/all-pole $6\\times6$ bracket family, the site-1 vacuum has no compact determinant form. The exact 12-state SoV sum (Direction 4) remains the representation, unless a genuinely different determinant shape (more rows or brackets) is used.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result 6b.** With the scale fixed, the best achievable relative residual is:\n- **0.766** with the $L=2$ w-vacuum Q's on ladder 1: a global scan over ladder-2 $F_1\\in\\mathbb P^3$, with the optimal $F_2$ for each, followed by local refinement that reaches the same value from 5 starts;\n- **0.774** with the $L=1$ w-vacuum Q's on ladder 1.\n\nSo **no** per-ladder $6\\times6$ of the form [ladder 1 = w-vacuum Q's, ladder 2 = any data] equals $\\langle\\Omega_w\\otimes e_1^T|\\Psi\\rangle$. A Q-form for the site-1 vacuum needs a different structure, for example modified ladder-1 data, mixed brackets, or a sum of determinants.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 8. Direction 5: reading the exact 12-state sum term by term (2026-10-09)\nSpec: `site1-Qform/5-bracket-decomposition.md`. The fitted determinant ansätze of §6–7 are negative; here the **exact** sum of §4 is rewritten in minimal variables and then read term by term for bracket structure.\n\n**Variables.** On ladder 1, $v(\\theta_1)\\parallel v(\\theta_1-h)$ and $v(\\theta_1-3h),v(\\theta_1-2h),v(\\theta_1-h)$ span a 2-plane. Per state $B$:\n- $\\lambda_s=v_k(\\theta_s)/v_k(\\theta_s-h)$ ($k$-independent), $s=1,2$;\n- $v(\\theta_1-h)=\\alpha\\,v(\\theta_1-3h)+\\beta\\,v(\\theta_1-2h)$.\n\nThen the 8 site-1 wavefunctions (normalized at the vacuum triple $(-3,-2,-1)$), in the `trip` order $(-3,-2,-1),(-3,-1,-1),(-2,-1,-1),(-3,-2,0),(-3,-1,0),(-3,0,0),(-2,-1,0),(-2,0,0)$, are\n$$\\psi^{(1)}=\\{1,\\ \\beta,\\ -\\alpha,\\ \\lambda_1,\\ \\lambda_1\\beta,\\ \\lambda_1^2\\beta,\\ -\\lambda_1\\alpha,\\ -\\lambda_1^2\\alpha\\},$$\nand the overlap of a general site-1 covector $\\sum_\\nu c_\\nu x_\\nu\\otimes e_1^T$ is a polynomial in $(\\alpha,\\beta,\\lambda_1,\\lambda_2)$, linear in the $c_\\nu$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 2-plane data per state: v(θ1-h) = α v(θ1-3h) + β v(θ1-2h); λs = v_k(θs)/v_k(θs-h) *)\nvv[B_, s_, m_] := colV2[B, s, m];\nabSolve[B_] := Module[{M = Transpose[{vv[B, 1, -3], vv[B, 1, -2]}], sol}, sol = LeastSquares[M, vv[B, 1, -1]]; {sol, Norm[M . sol - vv[B, 1, -1]]/Norm[vv[B, 1, -1]]}];\nabData = Table[abSolve[B], {B, nS}];\nchecks[\"v(θ1-h) in span{v(θ1-3h), v(θ1-2h)} (max residual)\"] = Max[abData[[All, 2]]];\nαB = abData[[All, 1, 1]]; βB = abData[[All, 1, 2]];\nλ1B = Table[vv[B, 1, 0][[1]]/vv[B, 1, -1][[1]], {B, nS}]; λ2B = Table[λ2[B], {B, nS}];\n(* the 8 site-1 wavefunctions in these variables, trip order *)\npsiAB[B_] := With[{a = αB[[B]], b = βB[[B]], l = λ1B[[B]]}, {1, b, -a, l, l b, l^2 b, -l a, -l^2 a}];\nchecks[\"8 site-1 wavefunctions = {1,β,-α}x{1,λ1,λ1²} (max rel dev)\"] = Max[Table[Abs[psi1[B, trip[[i]]]/psiAB[B][[i]] - 1], {B, nS}, {i, 8}]];\n(* symbolic polynomial: K entries rationalized (they are rational at this point, cf. Ktab); c[ν] free *)\ntripIdx[t_] := First[FirstPosition[trip, t]];\npsiSym = {1, β, -α, λ1, λ1 β, λ1^2 β, -λ1 α, -λ1^2 α};\nKrat[ν_] := {#[[1]], Rationalize[Chop[#[[2]], 10^-40], 10^-30]} & /@ Krow[ν];\nchecks[\"K rationalization error\"] = Max[Table[Abs[Krat[ν][[i, 2]] - Krow[ν][[i, 2]]], {ν, 8}, {i, Length[Krow[ν]]}]];\nWsym[ν_] := Sum[kx[[2]] psiSym[[tripIdx[kx[[1, 1]]]]] If[kx[[1, 2]] == {-3, -2, -1}, 1, λ2], {kx, Krat[ν]}];\nRsym = Sum[c[ν] Wsym[ν], {ν, 8}];\nsubsB[B_] := {α -> αB[[B]], β -> βB[[B]], λ1 -> λ1B[[B]], λ2 -> λ2B[[B]]};\n(* check against the exact overlap for the generic rotation of cell 18 (c = cL1) and for a random non-rotation covector *)\nSeedRandom[7]; cRnd = RandomInteger[{-9, 9}, 8];\nexactOvl[cvec_, B_] := (Flatten[KroneckerProduct[cvec . xL1, uv[1]]] . ketC[[B]])/(x0C . ketC[[B]]);\nchecks[\"Rsym = exact overlap, rotation c=cL1 (max rel dev)\"] = Max[Table[Abs[(Rsym /. Thread[Array[c, 8] -> cL1] /. subsB[B])/exactOvl[cL1, B] - 1], {B, nS}]];\nchecks[\"Rsym = exact overlap, random c (max rel dev)\"] = Max[Table[Abs[(Rsym /. Thread[Array[c, 8] -> cRnd] /. subsB[B])/exactOvl[cRnd, B] - 1], {B, nS}]];\nGrid[{#, N[checks[#], 3]} & /@ {\"v(θ1-h) in span{v(θ1-3h), v(θ1-2h)} (max residual)\", \"8 site-1 wavefunctions = {1,β,-α}x{1,λ1,λ1²} (max rel dev)\", \"K rationalization error\", \"Rsym = exact overlap, rotation c=cL1 (max rel dev)\", \"Rsym = exact overlap, random c (max rel dev)\"}, Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"368062\" data-output-id=\"22\" data-out-n=\"280\" data-sub-idx=\"23\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"59\" data-sub-start=\"23\" data-sub-end=\"23\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[280]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"14\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:6.04em;vertical-align:-2.75em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.29em;\"><span style=\"top:-5.25em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:6em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-2.75em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.25em;\"><span style=\"top:-5.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">v(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mord\">1-h) in span{v(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mord\">1-3h), v(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mord\">1-2h)} (max residual)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.21em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">8 site-1 wavefunctions = {1,</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.05278em;\">β</span><span class=\"mord\">,-</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span><span class=\"mord\">}x{1,</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span><span class=\"mord\">1,</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span><span class=\"mord\">1²} (max rel dev)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">K rationalization error</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.81em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">Rsym = exact overlap, rotation c=cL1 (max rel dev)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-0.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">Rsym = exact overlap, random c (max rel dev)</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.75em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:6em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-2.75em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.25em;\"><span style=\"top:-5.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.21em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0.</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">