   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Exact membership test.** The local family's image is a 4-dimensional cone in the 8-dimensional space of $\\psi$-coefficients. Its ideal (polynomial relations among the 8 coefficients $\\phi_\\nu$) is computed by elimination; a target vector lies in the (closure of the) image iff every generator vanishes on it. This replaces the numeric fit, which only gives upper bounds.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* elimination ideal: relations among the φ_ν(F) *)\nphs = Array[ph, 8];\nimgGB = TimeConstrained[GroebnerBasis[Join[Thread[phs - φofF]], Join[phs, Floc], Floc, MonomialOrder -> EliminationOrder], 400, $Failed];\nnGen = If[imgGB === $Failed, \"timed out\", Length[imgGB]];\n(* exact rational targets: K is rational, so c.K for a rational c is rational; the rotation cone is tested with random rational rotations built from (a, b), b.a = 0, via the inverse of X *)\nXlin = Table[Flatten[Xmat[UnitVector[8, k]]], {k, 8}];  (* 8 x 9: GT covector -> flattened X *)\nrotFromAB[a_, b_] := Module[{Xt = Flatten[Outer[Times, a, b]], φ}, φ = LinearSolve[Transpose[Xlin], Xt]; φ . Inverse[xL1]];  (* c-vector (x_ν basis) of the rotation with X = a b^T *)\nSeedRandom[23]; abList = Table[With[{a = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 3], b0 = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 3]}, {a, b0 - (b0 . a) a/(a . a)}], {3}];\nchecks[\"rotFromAB gives rotations (2nd/1st sv)\"] = Max[rank1dev[Xc[rotFromAB @@ ab]] & /@ abList];\nmemb[tgt_] := If[imgGB === $Failed, \"n/a\", Max[Abs[N[imgGB /. Thread[phs -> tgt], 20]]]/Max[1, Max[Abs[N[tgt, 20]]]^3]];\nmembTab = If[imgGB === $Failed, \"n/a\", Join[\n  {\"control: exact family member\" -> memb[φofF /. Thread[Floc -> {1, 2/3, -1/2, 3/7, 1/5, -2/9}]], \"control: random vector\" -> memb[RandomInteger[{-9, 9}, 8]]},\n  Table[With[{cr = rotFromAB @@ ab}, {\"group 1 (c.Kvac)\" -> memb[cr . Kvac], \"group 2 (c.K20)\" -> memb[cr . K20]}], {ab, abList}] // Flatten]];\nStringReplace[ToString[{nGen, N[checks[\"rotFromAB gives rotations (2nd/1st sv)\"], 3], membTab}, InputForm], \"\\n\" -> \" \"]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
