  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 9 — Conclusions (2026-10-09)\n1. **No contour-integral determinant with ladder-dependent vacuum data.** For $\\Omega_w\\otimes\\Omega_{w'}$ the full-measure $\\det_6$ with $F$ = $w$-vacuum Q's on ladder 1 and $w'$-vacuum Q's on ladder 2 fails (max relative deviation 24.9 with the L=2 vacuum Q's, 5.8 with the one-site ones, 6.1 mixed), while the sanity check $\\Omega_{w'}\\otimes\\Omega_{w'}\\propto\\det_6[F_{{\\rm vac},w'}]$ holds to $10^{-48}$. The per-ladder $\\det_6$ is the same determinant up to $(e^{2\\pi i\\theta_2/h}-e^{2\\pi i\\theta_1/h})^3$.\n2. **The SoV bra wavefunction of a product bra does not factorize.** Measure-free test $M_{ww'}M_{w'w}=M_{ww}M_{w'w'}$: relative deviation 1.6; $M_{ww'}/M_{ww}$ varies by a factor 46 over the site-1 triple. All four $8\\times8$ coefficient matrices have full rank 8 (even $M_{ww}$, so the SoV measure itself couples the ladders). Hence there is no 'sum over SoV contour integrals with a factorized bra wavefunction' for $g_1\\ne g_2$; the site-1 rotation is the $w_2\\to\\infty$ limit of this.\n\n**Net.** For site-local rotations the exact representations are lattice sums with explicit coefficient tables (12 states for site 1, 64 for $g_1\\otimes g_2$): brackets of non-factorizing multi-point kernels. A single contour-integral determinant would need a bracket structure beyond piecewise-vacuum bra data.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 10. The trick of 2603.26617 (App. G) for the gl(3) adjoint\nThere: $\\langle W^\\ell_{\\omega,\\kappa}\\otimes W^{L-\\ell}_\\omega|\\Psi\\rangle=K_\\kappa(\\tau)\\langle W_\\omega^L|\\Psi\\rangle$ with $K_\\kappa$ a ladder-$\\ell$ contour-bracket determinant (G7–G9), because $1-\\kappa t_+(\\theta_1)+\\kappa^2t_{[1,1]}(\\theta_1)$ **localizes** on site 1 and is diagonal on $|\\Psi\\rangle$. The result is a product of two *different* rotations of the vacuum, with overlap = (global det) × (ladder-1 det).\n\nHere, for $\\Lambda=(2,1,0)$, $L=2$, in the same spirit:\n- **Exp. 1.** Take $f_y(B)=\\det_2^{\\rm su(2)\\text{-like}}[Q_B;y]_{\\rm ladder\\,1}/{\\rm minor}_1$ (cell 68, the gl(3) analogue of (G7)), build the covector $\\Phi_y$ with $\\langle\\Phi_y|\\Psi_B\\rangle=f_y(B)\\langle\\Omega_w\\otimes\\Omega_w|\\Psi_B\\rangle$, and ask: is $\\Phi_y$ a product state, and are its factors rotations? Control: the global $\\det_4$ (both ladders) must give $\\Omega\\rho(D)\\otimes\\Omega\\rho(D)$. Also: is $f_y$ in the span of the localizing eigenvalues $\\{1,\\tau_{11},\\tau_{21}\\}$ at $\\theta_1-2h$?\n- **Exp. 2.** Localization of $T_\\lambda(\\theta_1-2h)$ on $\\langle\\Omega_w\\otimes\\Omega_w|$ (diagonal frame), and the exact solve for rotations in ${\\rm span}\\{\\Omega_1,\\Omega_1T^{(1)}_{11},\\Omega_1T^{(1)}_{21}\\}$ (the analogue of the $\\kappa$-family), and the same on the SoV vacuum $x_0$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Exp. 1: covector with prescribed overlaps f(B) <Ω|Ψ_B> (companion frame), product-state and rotation tests *)\novlΩ = Table[Flatten[KroneckerProduct[Ωc[wN], Ωc[wN]]] . ketC[[B]], {B, nS}];\ncovOf[f_List] := (f ovlΩ) . ketInvC;\nsvRel[φ_] := With[{s = SingularValueList[N[Partition[φ, d1], 30]]}, s/First[s]];\nfactors[φ_] := Module[{u, s, v}, {u, s, v} = SingularValueDecomposition[N[Partition[φ, d1], 30]]; {u[[All, 1]], Conjugate[v[[All, 1]]]}];\n(* control: global su(2)-like det4 (cell 10) -> Ωρ(D)⊗Ωρ(D) *)\nfGlob[y_] := Table[su2det4[B, y]/minor2s[B], {B, nS}];\nφG = covOf[fGlob[-6/5]];\nchecks[\"control: det6 x det4 covector is a product state (2nd/1st sv)\"] = svRel[φG][[2]];\nchecks[\"control: its two factors are rotations (2nd/1st sv of X)\"] = rank1dev /@ Xmat /@ factors[φG];\n(* ladder-1 su(2)-like det2 (cell 68) *)\nfL1[y_] := Table[su2det1[B, y]/minor1[B], {B, nS}];\nexp1 = Table[With[{φ = covOf[fL1[y]]}, {y, N[svRel[φ][[2 ;; 3]], 3], N[rank1dev /@ Xmat /@ factors[φ], 3]}], {y, {-6/5, 3, 7/4}}];\n(* is f_y in the span of the localizing eigenvalues at θ1-2h? (T2n from cell 14, diag frame kets vecS) *)\nτof[l_] := Table[With[{k = Ordering[Abs[vecS[[B]]], -1][[1]]}, (T2n[l] . vecS[[B]])[[k]]/vecS[[B, k]]], {B, nS}];\nτ11 = τof[{1, 1}]; τ21 = τof[{2, 1}]; τ10 = τof[{1, 0}]; τ20 = τof[{2, 0}];\nspanRes[f_, basis_] := Module[{A = Transpose[basis], c}, c = LeastSquares[A, f]; Norm[A . c - f]/Norm[f]];\nones = ConstantArray[1, nS];\nexp1span = Table[{y, N[spanRes[fL1[y], {ones, τ11, τ21}], 3], N[spanRes[fL1[y], {ones, τ11, τ21, τ11^2, τ11 τ21, τ21^2}], 3], N[spanRes[fL1[y], {ones, τ10, τ11, τ20, τ21}], 3], N[spanRes[fL1[y], {ones, τ10, τ11, τ20, τ20 τ11/τ10}], 3]}, {y, {-6/5, 3}}];\nStringReplace[ToString[{N[checks[\"control: det6 x det4 covector is a product state (2nd/1st sv)\"], 3], N[checks[\"control: its two factors are rotations (2nd/1st sv of X)\"], 3], exp1, exp1span}, InputForm], \"\\n\" -> \" \"]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
