  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 10 — Result (2026-10-09): a product of two distinct rotations with a contour-integral determinant overlap\nFor $\\Lambda=(2,1,0)$, $L=2$, ket twist $z$, companion-frame one-site vacua $\\Omega_{(p,q)}=e_1^TP(p,q)$ (cell 25), $y^*:=w_2\\,\\dfrac{\\theta_{12}-h}{\\theta_{12}-2h}$:\n$$v_2=\\Omega_{(w_1,y^*)},\\qquad v_1=\\Omega_{(w_1,y^*)}\\,\\rho\\big((w_2-G(z)^T)^{-1}\\big)=\\Omega_{(w_2,y^*)}\\,\\rho\\big((w_1-G(z)^T)^{-1}\\big),$$\n$$\\frac{\\langle v_1\\otimes v_2|\\Psi_B\\rangle}{\\langle x_0|\\Psi_B\\rangle}=c\\;\\frac{\\det_6N[Q_B,Q_{{\\rm vac},(w_1,w_2)}]}{\\Psi_Q^B(x_0)}\\;\\frac{\\det_{j\\in\\{3,2\\}}\\big[-\\langle Q^jE\\rangle_1,\\ \\langle Q^{j[-]}E\\rangle_1\\big]}{Q^2(\\theta_1-2h)Q^3(\\theta_1-3h)-Q^3(\\theta_1-2h)Q^2(\\theta_1-3h)},\\qquad E=y^{*\\,-x/h},$$\nwith $\\langle\\cdot\\rangle_1$ the bracket over the ladder-1 poles $\\theta_1-nh$, $n=0,1,2$, with the one-site weights (cell 68). State-independence of $c$: $10^{-50}$ on all 64 states (cell 102). Both factors are exact rotations and distinct. The state is the global vacuum of twist $(w_1,y^*)$ with a **site-1 resolvent rotation at $w_2$**, i.e. the structure $\\langle W_{\\omega,\\kappa}\\otimes W_\\omega|$ of 2603.26617 App.\\ G with $\\omega\\leftrightarrow(w_1,y^*)$, $\\kappa\\leftrightarrow1/w_2$; but the global det carries the $(w_1,w_2)$ vacuum Q's and the ladder det carries $y^*$ (the 'paper-like' assignment det$_6(w_1,y^*)\\times$det$_2(w_2)$ fails, 60.8).\n\n**How it was found (cells 86–102).** $T_{11},T_{21}$ at $\\theta_1-2h$ localize exactly on $\\langle\\Omega_w\\otimes\\Omega_w|$; $T_{10},T_{20}$ do not, but $\\langle\\Omega|T_\\lambda(\\theta_1-2h)=v_\\lambda\\otimes\\Omega_1+v'_\\lambda\\otimes\\omega_2$ with one fixed second site-2 direction $\\omega_2=\\Omega_{(w_1,z_2)}$ (exact), and the whole line $\\Omega_1+\\kappa\\omega_2$ lies in the rotation cone. In the 5-parameter family $\\langle\\Omega|(c_0+c_1T_{10}+c_2T_{11}+c_3T_{20}+c_4T_{21})$ the product locus has one component with $c_1,c_3\\neq0$, on which the site-1 factor is automatically a rotation; it is $z$-independent and equals $\\langle\\Omega|\\mathcal K_{y^*}$ where $\\mathcal K_y$ has eigenvalue the ladder-1 su(2)-like det ($f_y=4y^4-70y^3\\tau_{10}+y^2(\\ldots)+394y\\tau_{21}$ at this point). $y^*$ was decoded from runs at five $(h,\\theta,z,w)$ points (cells 97–100); $v_1$ from a scan over $\\Omega_{(p,q)}\\rho(M)$ (cell 101, residual 0).\n\n**Isolated extras.** $\\Omega_1T^{(1)}_{21}\\otimes\\Omega_1$ (overlap $\\tau_{21}\\det_6$) and $\\langle\\Omega|(e_1+e_8\\,t_2(\\theta_2+h)t_1(\\theta_2-h))$ at a fixed ratio are also products of rotations; no continuous family inside the linear span of transfer matrices at $\\theta_1-2h$, $\\theta_1$, $\\theta_2\\pm h$.\n\n**Open.** Second numeric point for the det identity itself (the structure and $y^*$ are checked at five points, the determinant only at P1); the general $(w_1,w_2,w_3)$ and $y_2$ dependence (here $y_2=\\infty$ on the resolvent); the $L>2$ / general-rep version (where the localizing set is larger).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* (1) the rationalized τ-expansion coefficients of f_y reproduce the 60-digit data? *)\ncRat = Rationalize[Chop[N[cPow, 20], 10^-30], 10^-18];\nchecks[\"τ-expansion: rational coefficients reproduce f_y to 60 digits (max abs dev)\"] = Max[Table[Max[Abs[basis5 . cRat[[p + 1]] - Coefficient[fyS, y, p]]], {p, 0, degY}]];\n(* (2) the coefficients A_k (of y^{4-?}τ_k) as monomials in h and (θ12 - k h): from the three (h,θ) points use c* ∝ c(y*): A0/A3 = c0/y*^2, A1/A3 = c1/y*, A2/A3 = c2, A4/A3 = c4 y* (c3 = 1) *)\npts = {{hN, thN[[1]] - thN[[2]], runH0}, {1/3, thN[[1]] - thN[[2]], runH1}, {hN, 1/5 + 4/9, runTh1}};\nratiosAt[run_] := Module[{c = \"c*\" /. run, ys = \"y*\" /. run}, {c[[1]]/ys^2, c[[2]]/ys, c[[3]], c[[5]] ys}];\ndata = Table[{p[[1]], p[[2]], ratiosAt[p[[3]]]}, {p, pts}];\n(* brute-force monomial search: ratio = C h^a (θ12-h)^b1 (θ12-2h)^b2 (θ12-3h)^b3 (θ12+h)^b4, exponents in -3..3, C fixed by point 1, exact check at points 2,3 *)\nmono[hh_, th_, {a_, b1_, b2_, b3_, b4_}] := hh^a (th - hh)^b1 (th - 2 hh)^b2 (th - 3 hh)^b3 (th + hh)^b4;\nexpo = Tuples[Range[-3, 3], 5];\nfindMono[k_] := Module[{r1 = data[[1, 3, k]], hits}, hits = Select[expo, Function[e, Module[{C = r1/mono[data[[1, 1]], data[[1, 2]], e]}, And @@ Table[C mono[data[[i, 1]], data[[i, 2]], e] == data[[i, 3, k]], {i, 2, 3}]]]]; {k, Table[{e, r1/mono[data[[1, 1]], data[[1, 2]], e]}, {e, hits}]}];\nmonoHits = Table[findMono[k], {k, 4}];\nStringReplace[ToString[{N[checks[\"τ-expansion: rational coefficients reproduce f_y to 60 digits (max abs dev)\"], 3], data, monoHits}, InputForm], \"\\n\" -> \" \"]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
