      {
       "data": "Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all \"solve\" variables.",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      },
      {
       "data": "{\n\t\"name\": \"WolframKernelMessage\",\n\t\"message\": \"Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all \\\"solve\\\" variables.\",\n\t\"stack\": \"\"\n}",
       "mime": "application/vnd.code.notebook.error"
      }
     ],
     "id": "be8dfcc6-9782-4387-8148-007e49563a40"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 11.4 a GENERIC rotation g on site 2 (not a vacuum): (a) write g = Ω_{(w1,y)} ρ(D) by an exact Solve at a fixed w1 (w1 is a torus direction, cell 108, so any w1 works); the solutions' y-values are the torus invariant(s) y(g). (b) Then the site-1 partner is g ρ((w2(y) - G^T)^-1) with w2(y) = y(θ12-2h)/(θ12-h), and the overlap is χ_μ(D) x det6[Q_vac,(w1,w2(y))]/Ψ_Q x det2^(1)[Q_B; y]/minor1. g is built from a rational Gauss decomposition (lower unipotent x torus x upper unipotent) so everything stays exact. *)\nSeedRandom[114]; gaussPars = RandomInteger[{-6, 6}, 6]/RandomInteger[{2, 7}, 6]; gaussD = {3/5, -7/4, 9/8};\ngRnd = x01 . MatrixExp[gaussPars[[1]] Ee[2, 1]] . MatrixExp[gaussPars[[2]] Ee[3, 1]] . MatrixExp[gaussPars[[3]] Ee[3, 2]] . ρdiag[gaussD] . MatrixExp[gaussPars[[4]] Ee[1, 2]] . MatrixExp[gaussPars[[5]] Ee[1, 3]] . MatrixExp[gaussPars[[6]] Ee[2, 3]];\nchecks[\"11.4 g is a rotation of x0 (all 2x2 minors of X vanish, exact)\"] = (Union[Flatten[Minors[Xdiag[gRnd], 2]]] === {0});\n(* (a) solve Ω_{(w1,y)}.ρdiag[d] = s g at two fixed w1's; compare the y's *)\nsolveTor[w1fix_] := Module[{eqs, sol}, eqs = Thread[(oneSiteVac[zN, {w1fix, yys, 3/5}] . ρdiag[{d1s, d2s, d3s}]) == sSc gRnd]; sol = Solve[eqs, {yys, d1s, d2s, d3s, sSc}]; Select[sol, (sSc /. #) =!= 0 &]];\n{solTorA, solTorB} = {solveTor[-7/3], solveTor[9/4]};\nchecks[\"11.4 number of solutions at w1 = -7/3 and 9/4\"] = Length /@ {solTorA, solTorB};\nchecks[\"11.4 y(g): the torus invariant(s), at the two w1's\"] = {Union[yys /. solTorA], Union[yys /. solTorB]};\n(* (b) end-to-end at the first solution (w1 = -7/3) *)\nsolT1 = First[solTorA]; yG = yys /. solT1; dG = {d1s, d2s, d3s} /. solT1; w2G = w2Of[yG];\ngPartner = gRnd . ρdiag[Dy[w2G]];\nchecks[\"11.4 Ω_{(w1,y)}ρ(D) reproduces g (exact)\"] = (MatrixRank[{oneSiteVac[zN, {-7/3, yG, 3/5}] . ρdiag[dG], gRnd}] == 1);\nΦG = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[gPartner, gRnd]]; ovlG = Table[(ΦG . vecS[[B]])/x0ovl[[B]], {B, nS}];\nFvG = vacQ[{-7/3, w2G, 3/5}];\nratG = If[FvG === $Failed, \"vac Q's not found\", Table[ovlG[[B]]/(charB[dG, B] (det6[B, FvG]/psiQ[B]) (su2det1[B, yG]/minor1[B])), {B, nS}]];\nchecks[\"11.4 MAIN: <gρ(D_{w2(y)})⊗g|Ψ> ∝ χ_μ(D) det6(w1,w2(y)) det2(y): state-independence (64 states)\"] = If[StringQ[ratG], ratG, Max[Abs[ratG/ratG[[1]] - 1]]];\nchecks[\"11.4 the partner is a rotation and distinct from g\"] = {Union[Flatten[Minors[Xdiag[gPartner], 2]]] === {0}, MatrixRank[{gPartner, gRnd}]};\nGrid[{{\"g rotation (exact)\", checks[\"11.4 g is a rotation of x0 (all 2x2 minors of X vanish, exact)\"]}, {\"# solutions at w1 = -7/3, 9/4\", checks[\"11.4 number of solutions at w1 = -7/3 and 9/4\"]}, {\"y(g) at the two w1's\", checks[\"11.4 y(g): the torus invariant(s), at the two w1's\"]}, {\"Ωρ(D) = g (exact)\", checks[\"11.4 Ω_{(w1,y)}ρ(D) reproduces g (exact)\"]}, {\"D, w2(y)\", {dG, w2G}}, {\"MAIN state-independence\", N[checks[\"11.4 MAIN: <gρ(D_{w2(y)})⊗g|Ψ> ∝ χ_μ(D) det6(w1,w2(y)) det2(y): state-independence (64 states)\"], 3]}, {\"partner rotation, rank{partner, g}\", checks[\"11.4 the partner is a rotation and distinct from g\"]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
