  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 11 — Result (2026-10-09, later): the §10 family is \"any rotation on site 2, one fixed resolvent on site 1\" (3-dimensional); no $\\kappa$-family; the mechanism does not iterate\n\n1. **Torus = character** (cell 108): $\\langle\\varphi\\rho(D)\\otimes\\psi\\rho(D)|\\Psi_B\\rangle=\\prod_i d_i^{\\mu_i(B)}\\langle\\varphi\\otimes\\psi|\\Psi_B\\rangle$ for arbitrary covectors (exact to 60 digits). This is why the global rotation of §2 is $\\det_6\\times\\det_4$: the $\\det_4$ is the character of a resolvent.\n2. **$w_1$ is a torus direction, $y$ a torus invariant** (cell 108; three generic points, exact rationals): rank of $\\partial(\\Omega_{(w_1,y)}\\rho(D))/\\partial(w_1,D)$ at fixed $y$ is 3 (= torus 2 + scale), with $y$ free it is 4 (= the whole orbit; 1-dim fibres whose tangent has zero $y$-component); $\\Omega_{(w_1,y)}/\\Omega_{(w_1',y)}$ is componentwise a torus character (residual 0). So the two-parameter family of §5.6b is really (torus direction, $y$). (The first run sat at $y=5/4=z_2$, where $\\Omega_{(w_1,y)}$ degenerates; generic points only.)\n3. **The $(w_1,y)$ family at fresh $w_1$** (cell 109): $(w_1,y)=(-7/3,7/5)$ and $(9/4,-2/3)$ give $\\det_6[(w_1,w_2(y))]\\times\\det_2^{(1)}(y)$ with state-independence $10^{-51}$ and $10^{-50}$ (all §10 determinant checks had $w_1=5/2$).\n4. **Generic rotation $g$ on site 2** (cell 111): $g=x_0\\,\\rho(\\text{lower unipotent}\\cdot\\text{torus}\\cdot\\text{upper unipotent})$ with random rationals. Exact `Solve` of $\\Omega_{(w_1,y)}\\rho(D)=g$ at $w_1=-7/3$ and $9/4$: exactly one solution each, the same $y(g)=1546301/1368484$. Partner $g\\,\\rho((w_2(y(g))-G^T)^{-1})$: overlap $\\propto\\chi_\\mu(D)\\,\\det_6N[Q_B,Q_{\\rm vac,(w_1,w_2(y(g)))}]/\\Psi_Q\\times\\det_2^{(1)}[Q_B;y(g)]/\\mathrm{minor}_1$, state-independent to $10^{-51}$ on 64 states; the partner is a rotation distinct from $g$.\n5. **Consequence.** The torus orbit of the §10 family is the 3-dimensional variety $V=\\{(g\\,\\rho(D_{w_2(y(g))}),\\,g):\\ g\\text{ a rotation of }x_0\\}$: for every site-2 rotation $g$, vacuum or not, exactly one site-1 partner. The vacua $\\Omega_w$ are not special (every $g$ is $\\Omega_{(w_1,y)}\\rho(D)$). The paper's continuous $\\kappa$-family does not exist for the adjoint even after allowing the torus. The general pair $(g_1,g_2)$ is 6-dimensional; $V$ has codimension 3 (missing: a free resolvent parameter and the second unipotent part of $g_1$ relative to $g_2$).\n6. **Iteration fails** (cell 110): with $\\Phi_0=v_1\\otimes v_2$ (the §10 state) as seed, $\\langle\\Phi_0|\\{1,T_{10},T_{11},T_{20},T_{21}\\}(\\theta_1-2h)$ have $8\\times8$ ranks $\\{1,4,3,8,8\\}$, the site-2 column space is all of $\\mathbb C^8$, and the exact product locus in the 5-dim span (784 quadrics, 9 s) is the seed alone. $T_{11},T_{21}$ do not localize on the deformed state, so the §10 step cannot be stacked on site 1 at $\\theta_1-2h$.\n7. **Open.** (a) Closed form of the invariant $y(g)$ (a projective invariant of $(a_ib_i)_i$ in the eigenbasis of $G$). (b) The site-2 analogue (insertions at $t_2(\\theta_2+h)$, $t_2(\\theta_2+h)t_1(\\theta_2-h)$ and their non-localizing partners) on the vacuum and on $V$. (c) Products of $T$'s at different points, or the joint site-1 $\\times$ site-2 span, as the remaining routes to a free resolvent / second unipotent parameter within single determinants. (d) Part A (§8) already shows that $(g_1,x_0)$ with generic $g_1$ is not a single natural determinant, so a 6-dimensional single-determinant family is unlikely; sums of determinants (two-ladder, with $\\lambda_2$ insertions) are the fallback.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 12 — Undoing the site-2 rotation: does the site-1 covector span every weight space? (adjoint, 2026-10-09 evening; spec `site1-Qform/7-undo-site2-rotation-span.md` §4)\n\nEvery rotation of the vacuum in the two-rotation family is $v_2=s\\,e_1^T\\rho(n)$ with $n\\in N_+$, and $\\rho(n)^{\\otimes2}$ fixes every highest-weight ket of $V\\otimes V$. So $\\langle v_1\\otimes v_2|\\nu,{\\rm HW}\\rangle=s\\langle\\varphi\\otimes e_1^T|\\nu,{\\rm HW}\\rangle$ with $\\varphi=v_1\\rho(n)^{-1}$, $v_1=v_2\\rho(\\Delta)$, $\\Delta={\\rm diag}(1/(\\omega-z_k))$, $\\omega=w_2(y)$. This is exact at finite twist. Below: per-weight ranks of $\\varphi(y)$, the closed forms for $n'=\\Delta^{-1}n\\Delta n^{-1}$, the highest-weight count, and the untwisting leading orders. Local names are prefixed `u12`; y-star never appears in comments with a closing bracket.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 12.1 setup (spec 4.1): Gauss element n(y) of the site-2 vacuum, rho(n) as an 8x8 matrix, v2 = e1^T rho(n), v1 = v2 rho(Delta), and the undone covector phi = v1 rho(n)^-1. Covectors are rows acted on from the right; in this convention the ket e1 is annihilated by Ee[i,j] with i<j (checked), so the raising operators are i<j. *)\nu12e1 = UnitVector[d1, 1]; u12w1 = -7/3; u12w3 = 3/5;\nu12rs[zz_, w1_, y_] := {(w1 - zz[[1]])/(w1 - zz[[2]]), ((w1 - zz[[1]]) (zz[[1]] - y) (zz[[2]] - zz[[3]]))/((zz[[1]] - zz[[2]]) (w1 - zz[[3]]) (y - zz[[3]])), ((w1 - zz[[2]]) (zz[[2]] - y) (zz[[1]] - zz[[3]]))/((zz[[1]] - zz[[2]]) (w1 - zz[[3]]) (zz[[3]] - y))};\nu12nMat[zz_, w1_, y_] := With[{rv = u12rs[zz, w1, y]}, {{1, rv[[1]], rv[[2]] + rv[[1]] rv[[3]]}, {0, 1, rv[[3]]}, {0, 0, 1}}];\nu12rN[zz_, w1_, y_] := With[{rv = u12rs[zz, w1, y]}, MatrixExp[rv[[1]] Ee[1, 2]] . MatrixExp[rv[[2]] Ee[1, 3]] . MatrixExp[rv[[3]] Ee[2, 3]]];\nu12rNinv[zz_, w1_, y_] := With[{rv = u12rs[zz, w1, y]}, MatrixExp[-rv[[3]] Ee[2, 3]] . MatrixExp[-rv[[2]] Ee[1, 3]] . MatrixExp[-rv[[1]] Ee[1, 2]]];\nu12Dy[zz_, yy_] := Table[1/(yy - zz[[i]]), {i, 3}];\nu12v2[zz_, w1_, y_] := oneSiteVac[zz, {w1, y, u12w3}];\nu12v1[zz_, w1_, y_] := u12v2[zz, w1, y] . ρdiag[u12Dy[zz, w2Of[y]]];\nu12phi[zz_, w1_, y_] := u12v1[zz, w1, y] . u12rNinv[zz, w1, y];\nchecks[\"12.1 ket e1 killed by Ee[i,j], i<j\"] = And @@ Flatten[Table[Ee[i, j] . u12e1 === ConstantArray[0, d1], {i, 3}, {j, i + 1, 3}]];\nchecks[\"12.1 v2 = e1^T rho(n) exactly (y = 7/5, -2/3, 3)\"] = And @@ Table[u12v2[zN, u12w1, yy] === u12e1 . u12rN[zN, u12w1, yy], {yy, {7/5, -2/3, 3}}];\nchecks[\"12.1 rho(n).rho(n)^-1 = 1 and rho(n) = rho of the 3x3 n (first-row entries)\"] = And[u12rN[zN, u12w1, 7/5] . u12rNinv[zN, u12w1, 7/5] === IdentityMatrix[d1], u12nMat[zN, u12w1, 7/5][[1]] === {1, u12rs[zN, u12w1, 7/5][[1]], u12rs[zN, u12w1, 7/5][[2]] + u12rs[zN, u12w1, 7/5][[1]] u12rs[zN, u12w1, 7/5][[3]]}];\n(* the same Dy as cell 10, evaluated at the resolvent point *)\nchecks[\"12.1 u12Dy = Dy (cell 10)\"] = u12Dy[zN, 3] === Dy[3];\nKeyTake[checks, {\"12.1 ket e1 killed by Ee[i,j], i<j\", \"12.1 v2 = e1^T rho(n) exactly (y = 7/5, -2/3, 3)\", \"12.1 rho(n).rho(n)^-1 = 1 and rho(n) = rho of the 3x3 n (first-row entries)\", \"12.1 u12Dy = Dy (cell 10)\"}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"607003\" data-output-id=\"42\" data-out-n=\"600\" data-sub-idx=\"15\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"113\" data-sub-start=\"15\" data-sub-end=\"15\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[600]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-line-broken=\"1\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:6em;vertical-align:-2.75em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"col-align-r\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.25em;\"><span style=\"top:-5.25em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.84em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.75em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.84em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.25em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.84em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-0.75em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.84em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.75em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"col-align-l\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.25em;\"><span style=\"top:-5.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">⟨</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">∣</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">12.1 ket e1 killed by Ee[i,j], i&lt;j</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.91em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">12.1 v2 = e1</span><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.25em;\"><span class=\"mord\">ˆ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">T rho(n) exactly (y = 7/5, -2/3, 3)</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">12.1 rho(n).rho(n)</span><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.25em;\"><span class=\"mord\">ˆ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">-1 = 1 and rho(n) = rho of the 3x3 n (first-row entries)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-0.91em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">12.1 u12Dy = Dy (cell 10)</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span><span class=\"mclose\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mclose\">⟩</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.75em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[600]= \\begin{aligned}\n  &\\langle\\!\\lvert \\text{12.1 ket e1 killed by Ee[i,j], i<j}\\to \\mathrm{True} \\\\\n  &,\\text{12.1 v2 = e1\\^{}T rho(n) exactly (y = 7/5, -2/3, 3)}\\to \\mathrm{True} \\\\\n  &,\\text{12.1 rho(n).rho(n)\\^{}-1 = 1 and rho(n) = rho of the 3x3 n (first-row entries)} \\\\\n  &\\to \\mathrm{True},\\text{12.1 u12Dy = Dy (cell 10)}\\to \\mathrm{True}\\rvert\\!\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "f42fe240-846d-4ce7-bb24-87a98d8bf0e5"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 12.2 highest-weight kets of V(x)V (spec 4.2): common null space of the total raising generators E1[i,j]+E2[i,j], i<j, taken per total-weight sector so each HW ket has a definite weight; then the exactness of the undo: (rho(n)(x)rho(n)).HW = HW and <v1(x)v2|HW> = s <phi(x)e1|HW>, s = first component of v2 (= <v2|e1>). *)\nu12raiseM = Join[E1[1, 2] + E2[1, 2], E1[1, 3] + E2[1, 3], E1[2, 3] + E2[2, 3]];\nu12sectors = GatherBy[Range[d2], wtBasis[[#]] &];\nu12HW = Flatten[Table[Module[{ns = NullSpace[u12raiseM[[All, sec]]]}, Table[Normal[SparseArray[Thread[sec -> v], {d2}]], {v, ns}]], {sec, u12sectors}], 1];\nu12HWwt = Table[wtBasis[[FirstCase[Range[d2], k_ /; v[[k]] =!= 0]]], {v, u12HW}];\nu12e12 = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[u12e1, u12e1]];\nchecks[\"12.2 number of HW kets = 6\"] = Length[u12HW];\nchecks[\"12.2 HW weights\"] = u12HWwt;\nchecks[\"12.2 HW kets annihilated by all total raising ops\"] = And @@ (u12raiseM . # === ConstantArray[0, 3 d2] & /@ u12HW);\nchecks[\"12.2 (rho(n)(x)rho(n)).HW = HW exactly (y = 7/5, -2/3)\"] = And @@ Table[With[{R = KroneckerProduct[u12rN[zN, u12w1, yy], u12rN[zN, u12w1, yy]]}, And @@ (R . # === # & /@ u12HW)], {yy, {7/5, -2/3}}];\nchecks[\"12.2 <v1(x)v2|HW> = s <phi(x)e1|HW> exactly (y = 7/5, -2/3, 3)\"] = And @@ Table[With[{v2 = u12v2[zN, u12w1, yy], v1 = u12v1[zN, u12w1, yy], ph = u12phi[zN, u12w1, yy]}, And @@ (Flatten[KroneckerProduct[v1, v2]] . # === v2[[1]] Flatten[KroneckerProduct[ph, u12e1]] . # & /@ u12HW)], {yy, {7/5, -2/3, 3}}];\nGrid[{{\"# HW kets\", checks[\"12.2 number of HW kets = 6\"]}, {\"HW weights\", checks[\"12.2 HW weights\"]}, {\"annihilated by raising\", checks[\"12.2 HW kets annihilated by all total raising ops\"]}, {\"rho(n)(x)rho(n) fixes HW\", checks[\"12.2 (rho(n)(x)rho(n)).HW = HW exactly (y = 7/5, -2/3)\"]}, {\"<v1(x)v2|HW> = s<phi(x)e1|HW>\", checks[\"12.2 <v1(x)v2|HW> = s <phi(x)e1|HW> exactly (y = 7/5, -2/3, 3)\"]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
