  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 12 — Result (2026-10-09, evening): undoing the site-2 rotation, adjoint\n\n1. **Exact undo.** $v_2=e_1^T\\rho(n(y))$, $n\\in N_+$, and $\\rho(n)^{\\otimes2}$ fixes the 6 highest-weight kets exactly (cell 115), so $\\langle v_1\\otimes v_2|{\\rm HW}\\rangle=s\\,\\langle\\varphi\\otimes e_1^T|{\\rm HW}\\rangle$ with $\\varphi=v_1\\rho(n)^{-1}=\\delta^\\Lambda e_1^T\\rho(n')$, $n'=\\Delta^{-1}n\\Delta n^{-1}$ (verified exactly with $y$ symbolic).\n2. **Per-weight ranks (weights of $V=(2,1,0)$-adjoint: dims 1,1,1,2,1,1,1).** Numeric (12 $y$'s), exact-in-$y$ (numerator coefficient vectors), and union over $w_1\\in\\{-7/3,9/4,5/2\\}$ are all equal to $\\dim V_\\mu$: **all 8 directions are spanned, no component vanishes identically.** Control with the resolvent point set to $y$ itself ($\\omega=y$): ranks $(0,1,0,1,1,1,1)$ for $\\mu=(0,1,2),(0,2,1),(1,0,2),(1,1,1),(1,2,0),(2,0,1),(2,1,0)$, i.e. the $(0,1,2)$ and $(1,0,2)$ components vanish identically and the 2-dim weight space is only hit once.\n3. **Closed forms (exact, $y$ symbolic).** $b'/(a'c')=(y-\\omega)/(y-z_2)$ with $\\omega=w_2(y)$; $a',b',c'$ agree with the spec formulas; $b'\\equiv0$ when $\\omega\\to y$ (the old blind spot). Mechanism: $b'\\neq0$ because $w_2(y)\\neq y$ (zero only at the isolated point $y=0$ at this numeric $z,\\theta,h$). **Deviation from spec §3(iii):** the $(0,1,2)$ (singlet-direction) component is $3\\,b'(a'c'-b')\\,\\delta^\\Lambda$ (relative to the $e_1$-normalized covector), not $\\propto b'(b'+a'c')$; $a'^2c'^2$ does not occur. It is nonzero for generic $y$. All other components agree with §3(iii).\n4. **HW count.** At fixed $w_1$ and torus $D=1$ the $12\\times6$ matrix $\\langle\\varphi(y_i)\\otimes e_1^T|{\\rm HW}_\\nu\\rangle$ has rank **5**, not 6 (per-irrep column ranks $1,1,1,2,1$, the singlet column is nonzero). The single null vector sits on the columns $(4,1,1)$, $(3,3,0)$ and the two octets (the functions $a',c',b',a'c'$ of $y$ satisfy one linear relation, rank 3). The union over three $w_1$ gives rank **6**, and the torus-completed family (the full 3-parameter family: $v\\to v\\rho(D)$ on both sites multiplies column $\\nu$ by $\\prod D_i^{\\nu_i}$, checked exactly) gives rank **6**, all irreps including the singlet and both octets (octet pair rank 2). Control $\\omega=y$: rank 4 even torus-completed (singlet missing and one octet direction lost).\n5. **Untwisting** $z_k=1+\\epsilon\\varphi_k$: leading orders $\\epsilon^0,\\epsilon^1,\\epsilon^1,\\epsilon^2$ (rank 2 over $y$)$,\\epsilon^3,\\epsilon^3,\\epsilon^4$ for $(2,1,0),(1,2,0),(2,0,1),(1,1,1),(0,2,1),(1,0,2),(0,1,2)$, as predicted.\n6. **Comparison with 2026-09-23** (reached only weights with $\\mu_3\\le\\lambda_2$, 5/6 HW, singlet missed): here the singlet direction is reached and the full family reaches 6/6. The mechanism is the shift $w_2(y)\\ne y$ of the resolvent point, which makes $b'\\neq0$.",
